OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773166943
OL,1,Vk4                               G7/21
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGFIRST GULF TROOPS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGRETURN TO BRITAIN
OL,4,D
OL,5, The first British servicemen and women
OL,6, have arrived back home from the Gulf.
OL,7,F
OL,8,FMore than 300 servicemen and women,
OL,9,Fmost of them reservists from 4626 Air
OL,10,FEvacuation Squadron, flew into RAF
OL,11,FBrize Norton, Oxfordshire.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FAbout 250 service personnel from a
OL,14,FTerritorial Army general hospital
OL,15,Farrived at Prestwick airport, Ayrshire.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FSix British prisoners of war - all from
OL,18,Fthe RAF - also returned from the Gulf.
OL,19,FTwo arrived at RAF Markham, Norfolk and
OL,20,Ftwo each at RAF Laarbruch and RAF
OL,21,FBruggen in Germany.
OL,22,D
OL,23,D]FFromG10-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
