OL,1,Vk4                               G8/21
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGHUGE ANTI-GOVERNMENT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGPROTEST IN MOSCOW
OL,4,D
OL,5, Hundreds of thousands of people rallied
OL,6, in Moscow today to back Boris Yeltsin,
OL,7, who has urged democrats to "declare
OL,8, war" on President Gorbachev.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FIn what was thought to be the biggest
OL,11,Fanti-government protest since 1917, the
OL,12,Fdemonstrators called for Mr Gorbachev
OL,13,Fto resign and heard calls for anti-
OL,14,FCommunist political groups to be formed
OL,15,F
OL,16,FA "no" vote in next week's referendum
OL,17,Fon preserving the USSR was urged.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FSackfuls of roubles were collected to
OL,20,Fsupport striking miners who want higher
OL,21,Fpay and the resignation of Mr Gorbachev
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG10-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
